{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791032175,"nonce":"bbH7Z6yFND4/HUmEqQl/xI2M+hI=","title":"the API cannot pace drawing by the Wayland frame callback","message":"ashui (2026-10-03, ashui git-bug 943a8797dd2bb1858b569b1ee83bbedf0245dc43fc3d0e3b8fa2ce339dab37b2) drew faster than the display refresh on GNOME Wayland. Mesa's WSI queued presents ahead of the compositor, and mutter then held them for a second at a time, giving about 3 fps under lavapipe. Pacing by the compositor's frame callback needs winit's Window::pre_present_notify, which the API did not have.\n\nDone in 93034bf2a05f663697b6424fb689e4477ff34340: Window.prePresentNotify(), called just before presenting. On Wayland the next RedrawRequested then waits for that frame's callback; elsewhere it does nothing, and in a page the agent already answers redraws at requestAnimationFrame. The desktop test's \"redraws paced by presented frames\" check (notify, present, requestRedraw, RedrawRequested arrives, three times) passes in CI run 37124189419 under sway, X11 and Windows. hlwindow 0c9d1a19b4aa5e82c96b6414de122f9f0be76ed8 moves to it.","files":null}]}